# Not written:
#   Never to the blocklist (floating) 2: references 'Geo_block': an alias of type 'geoip' (the countries of a GeoIP database), whose addresses are not in the configuration; the destination 'Geo_block' holds members only its platform knows; a rule of Google Cloud names addresses
#   Guests never to the blocklist: not converted: it matches the source of traffic that leaves, which is the source after outbound NAT
#   Voice from the partner - pass: the source of the rule is in zone WAN, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind WAN with --zone-network
#   VPN users to the web servers: the source of the rule is in zone OpenVPN, VPNSITE, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind OpenVPN, VPNSITE with --zone-network
#   Inside may ping (old kind): the source of the rule is in zone LAN, DMZ, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind LAN, DMZ with --zone-network
#   Default allow LAN to any rule: the source of the rule is in zone LAN, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind LAN with --zone-network
#   Web publishing: the source of the rule is in zone WAN, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind WAN with --zone-network
#   DMZ anywhere but LAN (disabled): the source of the rule is in zone DMZ, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind DMZ with --zone-network
#   DMZ ICMPv6: the source of the rule is in zone DMZ, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind DMZ with --zone-network
#   Servers fetch updates: the source of the rule is in zone DMZ, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind DMZ with --zone-network; the destination 'Updates' holds members only its platform knows; a rule of Google Cloud names addresses
#   Servers fetch updates 2: the source of the rule is in zone DMZ, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind DMZ with --zone-network
#   Servers fetch updates 3: the source of the rule is in zone DMZ, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind DMZ with --zone-network; the destination 'Updates' holds members only its platform knows; a rule of Google Cloud names addresses
#   Servers fetch updates 4: the source of the rule is in zone DMZ, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind DMZ with --zone-network
#   Guests to the portal (no protocol, both IP versions): the source of the rule is in zone GUEST, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind GUEST with --zone-network
#   DMZ anywhere but LAN (disabled) 2: the source of the rule is in zone DMZ, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind DMZ with --zone-network
#   Guests interactive (tos): not converted: it matches the type of service (tos) '0x10'; the source of the rule is in zone GUEST, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind GUEST with --zone-network
#   VPN users to LAN web (old kind): the source of the rule is in zone OpenVPN, VPNSITE, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind OpenVPN, VPNSITE with --zone-network
#   SSH to bastion (rule the port forward registers): the source of the rule is in zone WAN, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind WAN with --zone-network
#   Time for everyone (floating, not quick): the source of the rule is in zone WAN, LAN, DMZ, GUEST, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind WAN, LAN, DMZ, GUEST with --zone-network
